<title>USA: Ashland sees Nigerian go ahead this year.</title>
<headline>Ashland sees Nigerian go ahead this year.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-10-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Ashland Inc and Total SA are likely to begin development of the Okwori prospect offshore Nigeria during fiscal 1997, Ashland chief executive Paul W. Chellgren told securitiy analysts Monday.</p>
<p>He said the joint venture &quot;drilled two successful wells&quot; on the prospect during the year ended September 30 following the discovery well drilled in 1995.</p>
<p>Chellgren also said Ashland's crude oil reserves increased during fiscal 1996 and its natural gas reserves increased 14 percent to 577 billion cubic feet.</p>
<p>-- Jim Brumm 212-859-1710.</p>
